Try every session cookie instead of only the first one

The upstream backend picks the first LuCI session cookie it finds
("sysauth_http", then "sysauth_https", then "sysauth") and validates only
that one. A browser can hold a stale "sysauth_http" next to a valid
"sysauth_https": the http cookie is not Secure, so it survives an https
login and keeps being sent on every request. The stale cookie then shadows
the valid session and the backend answers every request with
invalid_session ("LuCI 登录状态无效或已过期") even though a valid session
is present.

The patch collects every candidate session id and tries them until rpcd
accepts one.

